hadiths[10]{hadithnumber,text}:
"882","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that two men claimed ownership of a livestock animal and both presented two witnesses each. So, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, decided that it should be divided equally between them."
"883","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “Whoever departs from obedience and separates from the community dies the death of ignorance. Whoever fights under a blind banner, becoming angry for the sake of tribalism, calling towards tribalism, and is killed, then he dies the death of ignorance. And whoever rebels against my Ummah, striking the righteous and the wicked among them, not sparing a believer due to his faith, nor honoring any covenant with a covenant-holder, then he is not from me, and I am not from him.”"
"884","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever withdraws from obedience and separates from the congregation dies the death of ignorance, and whoever takes up the sword against my Ummah, striking the righteous and the wicked alike, and does not honor the covenant of anyone who has a covenant, he is not from my Ummah. And whoever is killed under a blind banner, showing anger for tribalism, fighting for tribalism, and calling towards tribalism, if he dies, he dies the death of ignorance."
"885","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""The prophets of the Children of Israel used to lead them politically as well. Whenever a prophet passed away, another prophet would succeed him. But there will be no prophet after me."" They asked: O Messenger of Allah! Then what will happen? He said: ""There will be caliphs (deputies) and they will be many. Fulfill their rights, and ask Allah for your own rights."
"886","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""There will be no prophet after me."" They asked: O Messenger of Allah! Then what will happen? He (peace be upon him) said: ""There will be deputies one after another, so whoever among them remains upright, be loyal to their pledge of allegiance, and whoever does not remain upright, give them their due right, and ask Allah for your own right."
"887","Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: I asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! How will this matter (caliphate) be after you?"" He (peace be upon him) said: ""As long as there is goodness in your people, this matter will remain among your people."" I asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! Which of the Arabs will perish the soonest?"" He (peace be upon him) said: ""Your people."" I asked, ""How is that?"" He (peace be upon him) said: ""Death will be deemed lawful for them and envy towards people."
"888","Lady Umm al-Husayn (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: I saw the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) delivering a sermon in the plain of Arafat. He was saying: ""If a mutilated-nosed, Abyssinian slave is appointed as your leader, then listen to him and obey him, as long as he upholds the religion of Allah among you."
"889","It is narrated from Sayyidah Umm al-Husayn (may Allah be pleased with her) that she heard the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) saying similar to the previous narration."
"890","Lady Umm al-Husayn (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) during the Farewell Pilgrimage, he was delivering a sermon to the people, and he was wearing a cloak, which he had wrapped under his armpit, and the muscle of his arm was trembling. And I heard him (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Listen and obey, even if a slave with a mutilated nose and ears, an Abyssinian, is appointed as your leader/ruler over you, as long as he establishes the Book of Allah among you."
"891","Sayyidah Umm al-Husayn (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), then the narrator mentioned similar to the previous hadith."
